i.github.com/users/bikemurt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-02T15:19:28Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T15:35:03Z","body":"Just chiming in here as I do a lot of asset importing stuff and I do use the \"Extract Once\" feature quite a lot (for those who don't know, it has many [workflow benefits](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pMZ8TfbhdY8)).\n\n@YeldhamDev The core issue is that extracting materials will cause the `mat_id` to be unlinked from the GLTF file, so that PR (#115528) is incompatible with the extracting workflow.\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/549d1846bdfc0886b4696a1a76f15206364f69b0/editor/import/3d/resource_importer_scene.cpp#L1614\n\nThe `mat_id` from the import won't match after the material has been extracted.\n\nEdit: After looking for a few more minutes, now I'm unsure. I don't really know where `p_material_data` comes from,\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/549d1846bdfc0886b4696a1a76f15206364f69b0/editor/import/3d/resource_importer_scene.cpp#L3292","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4867356194/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]